// Your Supabase project. Copy this file to `Secrets.xcconfig`, which is
// gitignored, and fill in your own values:
//
//     cp Secrets.example.xcconfig Secrets.xcconfig
//
// Leave it empty and the app still runs — the library, the recipe editor and
// every Bluetooth feature are local. Only sync and the AI features need a
// project. See INSTALLATION.md.
//
// The publishable key is meant to be readable by a client; Row Level Security
// is what protects your rows. It is still worth keeping out of a public
// repository, because anyone holding it can create an account in your project
// and spend your AI quota.

// The host only. `//` in an xcconfig starts a comment, so the scheme is added
// back in code rather than written here.
SUPABASE_HOST =
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY =
